  "summary_en": "Japan's annual science, technology and innovation strategy for 2025, implementing the Sixth STI Basic Plan and previewing the Seventh. It prioritises AI, including physical AI and general-purpose AI robots, alongside quantum, fusion, space, and economic security. It also covers AI governance under the AI Act, the AI Safety Institute, and the Hiroshima AI Process.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Promote R&D and implementation of general-purpose AI robots and foundation models for AI robots, with GPU and synthetic-data infrastructure.",
   "Establish AI Strategic Headquarters and AI Basic Plan under the 2025 AI Act; study responsibility allocation for AI accidents.",
   "AI Safety Institute to develop verification tools and harmonise internationally; Hiroshima AI Process and Code of Conduct promoted.",
   "Review systems in high-impact fields such as medicine and automated driving as needed; expand UAS lines and CAV corridors.",
   "New International Standards Strategy with eight strategic domains including digital/AI and mobility."
